00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,390
This Hell-tier grid begins with one sharp choice.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:09,230
In Box Four, nine has only two possible homes: row five, column one, or row six, column two.

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,010
Let's test the lower position: row six, column two.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,460
Now follow the chain. The trial forces ordinary placements across the grid.

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,410
Row three now holds two sevens. Contradiction.

6
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:34,850
That trial fails. The other position is certain: row five, column one, is nine.

7
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,840
Two more placements follow.

